  "notes": "FR03-F5-W6 permanent physical-cell suite over the certified W6 artifacts (SVD fp64, FFT fp32, sparse-CG fp32). Readiness is the same VecRegClass geometry as W5: numPhysVecRegs=48, NumVecRegs=44, dynamic slots 44..47, special 32..43 excluded; target 0 is V0's normal initial physical cell. Static evidence: gem5 default MIDR 0x410fd070 (Cortex-A57) makes glibc's __libc_memset_ifunc fall through to __memset_generic, whose prologue is `dup v0.16b, w1`; native gdb breakpoint runs show libc memset is invoked 2-3 times per W6 program even though the kernels themselves are scalar FP64/FP32 (static arrays, no calloc). SVD keeps vec_lane_width=64 (fp64 data domain); FFT/sparse-CG use 32. Masks are lane-relative, SA1 on bits memset drives to zero, and fit both widths. Golden arrays/binary/source hashes, inputs and tolerances are unchanged from w6-fp-v1-f5; NaN/Inf/truncated/missing dumps fail through fsu_w6_oracle, and the golden never participates in the injection run. Target selection never depends on a fault-run SDC outcome; generation is identity only and never clears the permanent cell. Gate-phase revision 2026-11-04: target phys 0 (V0/libc memset) crashed with truncated evidence; switched to dynamic-pool slot 47 (highest allocatable dynamic Vec slot) using no-fault PRF geometry and a retry-pacing fix. This is a gate design correction before formal freeze, not an SDC-driven target search. Gate-phase revision: W6 seed2 mask 0x40000000 SA1 lane1 failed chain certification on SVD/sparse (L5 generation not activated); changed to sign SA1 lane1, matching the already-passing sign-SA1 mechanism but a distinct lane.",
  "suite_hash": "3b946a51ffb67e2086ed6df32395e90cd54c2d7dcf791654fb5e0312e61c172e"
